    "raw": "Let's denote the number of treats Jane brings as \\( T \\). According to the problem, Jane brings 75% as many pieces of bread as treats, so the number of pieces of bread Jane brings is \\( 0.75T \\).\n\nWanda brings half as many treats as Jane, so the number of treats Wanda brings is \\( \\frac{T}{2} \\). Wanda also brings three times as many pieces of bread as treats, and we know she brings 90 pieces of bread. Therefore, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 3 \\times \\frac{T}{2} = 90 \\]\nSolving for \\( T \\):\n\\[ \\frac{3T}{2} = 90 \\]\n\\[ 3T = 180 \\]\n\\[ T = 60 \\]\n\nSo, Jane brings 60 treats. Since Jane brings 75% as many pieces of bread as treats, the number of pieces of bread Jane brings is:\n\\[ 0.75 \\times 60 = 45 \\]\n\nWanda brings half as many treats as Jane, which is:\n\\[ \\frac{60}{2} = 30 \\]\nAnd Wanda brings 90 pieces of bread.\n\nNow, we can find the total number of pieces of bread and treats that Wanda and Jane brought to the zoo:\n\\[ \\text{Total pieces of bread} = 45 + 90 = 135 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total treats} = 60 + 30 = 90 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total pieces of bread and treats} = 135 + 90 = 225 \\]\n\nThus, the total number of pieces of bread and treats that Wanda and Jane brought to the zoo is 225.\n\nFINAL: 225",
